@page "/guides"
@inherits LiveComponentBase
@using MudBlazor
@using Waymark.Core.Guides
@using Waymark.Host.Components.Shared
@using Waymark.Host.Ui

<PageFrame Title="Host prompt" Lead="The first thing a connected agent reads about Waymark, and the one place where you speak to every agent at once.">
    <section class="wm-card" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
        <h2 id="about-heading" class="wm-card-title">What this is</h2>
        <p>When an agent connects, Waymark asks it to load a short <strong>overview</strong> before its first tool call. Waymark writes that overview itself. It has four parts:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>what each group of tools is for (code, packages, files, commands), and how an agent asks for the group's own guide;</li>
            <li>a few rules: a refusal is a decision, not a glitch; never write a hidden-secret marker into a file; what to do if a secret shows up;</li>
            <li>what is different right now: tools switched off, workspaces, the commands that ask you first, and the flows Claude has saved (their ids, names and one-line summaries);</li>
            <li>how to reuse earlier work: before it explores a feature an agent reads the flow saved for it (<code>recall</code>), and after it explores one it saves a flow (<code>memorise</code>). You read and prune the flows on the <strong>Flows</strong> page of each workspace.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The details of the tools, shells, approvals and long-running commands live in the group guides, which are built into Waymark and update with it. <strong>You do not edit any of that.</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Your text below is placed inside the overview</strong>, under &ldquo;Instructions from the owner&rdquo;, and wins wherever it disagrees with Waymark's defaults. Waymark's gates and approvals still apply, whatever the text says.</p>
        <p class="wm-muted">Good things to write: how you like work done, your conventions and project rules, what to ask before touching, what never to do, and your own workflows: a script the project ships, how to run it, and when to stop and wait for you. Agents load the overview once per conversation. After you save, every agent that holds the old text is told on its next call. Do not put secrets here: every agent that loads it receives it.</p>
    </section>

    @if (_error is not null)
    {
        <InlineAlert Severity="Severity.Error">@_error</InlineAlert>
    }

    <section class="wm-card" aria-labelledby="owner-heading">
        <div class="wm-row spread">
            <h2 id="owner-heading" class="wm-card-title">Your instructions</h2>
            <div class="wm-row">
                @if (_saved.ChangedUtc is null)
                {
                    <WmStatus State="StatusState.Off" Text="Empty" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <WmStatus State="StatusState.Healthy" Text="In use" />
                }
                <WmTag Text="@($"Your text: about {DisplayFormat.Count(_draftTokens)} tokens")" />
                <WmTag Text="@($"Whole overview as sent: about {DisplayFormat.Count(_overviewTokens)} tokens")" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="wm-muted wm-note">@HolderText()</p>
        <textarea class="wm-input wm-mono wm-textarea" rows="24" spellcheck="false" maxlength="@(HostPromptRules.MaxOwnerChars + 2_000)"
                  aria-label="Your instructions for every connected agent" placeholder="@Placeholder"
                  value="@_draft" @oninput="e => OnInput(e.Value?.ToString())" disabled="@_busy"></textarea>
        <div class="wm-row spread">
            <span class="wm-muted">@DisplayFormat.Count(DraftChars) of @DisplayFormat.Count(HostPromptRules.MaxOwnerChars) characters</span>
            <span class="wm-muted">@LastChange()</span>
        </div>
        @if (_draftTokens > HostPromptRules.WarnTokens)
        {
            <InlineAlert Severity="Severity.Warning">Every agent that loads the overview reads all of this. Past a few thousand tokens it starts to crowd out the work; consider trimming.</InlineAlert>
        }
        <div class="wm-row wm-card-actions">
            <WmButton Kind="ButtonKind.Primary" OnClick="SaveAsync" Disabled="@(_busy || !IsDirty || TooLong)">Save</WmButton>
            <WmButton OnClick="Revert" Disabled="@(_busy || !IsDirty)">Undo edits</WmButton>
            <WmButton Kind="ButtonKind.Danger" OnClick="ClearAsync" Disabled="@(_busy || _saved.ChangedUtc is null)">Clear my instructions</WmButton>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wm-card" aria-labelledby="preview-heading">
        <div class="wm-row spread">
            <h2 id="preview-heading" class="wm-card-title">What agents receive</h2>
            <WmButton OnClick="() => _showPreview = !_showPreview">@(_showPreview ? "Hide" : "Show")</WmButton>
        </div>
        <p class="wm-muted wm-note">The overview exactly as saved, with the live setup of this moment. Your text sits under &ldquo;Instructions from the owner&rdquo;.</p>
        @if (_showPreview)
        {
            <pre class="wm-mono wm-preview">@_preview</pre>
        }
    </section>

    <section class="wm-card" aria-labelledby="groups-heading">
        <h2 id="groups-heading" class="wm-card-title">Group guides</h2>
        <p class="wm-muted">Each group of tools also has a manual that is built into Waymark and updates with it, so there is nothing to edit. An agent asks for one when it first uses the group, so a group it never uses costs nothing.</p>
        <div class="wm-table-wrap">
            <table class="wm-table">
                <caption class="visually-hidden">Group guides</caption>
                <thead><tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">Size when sent</th><th scope="col">Who holds it</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var guide in _groupGuides)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td class="wm-capitalize">@guide.Module</td>
                            <td>About @DisplayFormat.Count(TokensOf(guide)) tokens</td>
                            <td>@GroupHolders(guide)</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
</PageFrame>
